{
  "comment": [
    "The contract between two runtimes computing one neighbourhood.",
    "assets/webapp/ego.js (egoStats) is the browser's Burt arithmetic;",
    "chitragupta/enrich/topic_brokerage.py computes the same numbers",
    "with networkx (effective_size, constraint) and stores them in the",
    "artefact (#713). The two conventions were verified equal before",
    "this file was written; these rows keep them equal -- node asserts",
    "egoStats reproduces every row (tests/webapp/ego.test.js), pytest",
    "asserts the networkx side does (tests/test_enrich_topic_brokerage",
    ".py), so neither can drift alone. Values were generated by the",
    "networkx side and cross-checked against a hand port of egoStats."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a broker: alters that never touch each other",
      "labels": [
        "E",
        "a",
        "b",
        "c"
      ],
      "edges": {
        "overlap": [
          {
            "a": "E",
            "b": "a",
            "overlap_coeff": 0.9
          },
          {
            "a": "E",
            "b": "b",
            "overlap_coeff": 0.6
          },
          {
            "a": "E",
            "b": "c",
            "overlap_coeff": 0.3
          }
        ],
        "semantic": []
      },
      "ego": "E",
      "expected": {
        "overlap": {
          "degree": 3,
          "ego_density": 0.0,
          "effective_size": 3.0,
          "constraint": 0.388889
        },
        "semantic": {
          "degree": 0,
          "ego_density": null,
          "effective_size": 0,
          "constraint": null
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a theme: a closed triangle plus an outside pull",
      "labels": [
        "E",
        "a",
        "b",
        "d"
      ],
      "edges": {
        "overlap": [
          {
            "a": "E",
            "b": "a",
            "overlap_coeff": 0.9
          },
          {
            "a": "E",
